{
  "_comment": "Ruby naming for the AWS CDK assembly closure \u2014 the JSII_RUBY_TARGET_CONFIG overlay consumed by src/target-config.ts. Upstream repos do not carry targets.ruby (external-language config never lands in an AWS repo), so the naming arrives at generation time via this file. Values are LOAD-BEARING: they become published gem and module names (permanent public API). Migrated from the fork-era publish pipeline's config (blog/.github/publish-config), which patched the same values into forked package.json files.",
  "aws-cdk-lib": {
    "_decisions": {
      "acronyms": "acronym casing is case-restoring over PascalCase segmentation; submodule names are DERIVED from these plus the aws_-prefix drop (aws_s3 -> AWSCDK::S3), so a new acronym-named service landing upstream without an entry here renders PascalCase (aws_xyz -> Xyz) until added \u2014 scripts/check-cdk-naming.js flags new submodules per release.",
      "FSX": "deliberately FSX, not AWS's FSx branding: mixed-case tokens (like IPv4) are only used where explicitly declared; module aws-fsx renders FSX. Changing this later renames published constants \u2014 breaking.",
      "v2/V2": "version suffixes stay lowercase v2/v6 in gem names (aws-cdk-asset-node-proxy-agent-v6) and module casing follows PascalCase segmentation (V2 only where an acronym or explicit module name declares it). Matches dotnet's convention.",
      "submodules": "explicit per-submodule modules harvested from the fork branch .jsiirc files (329 entries, the original naming decisions) plus entries added per release when scripts/check-cdk-naming.js flags new submodules. 2026-08-08 additions: ControlCatalog, DataExchange, Outposts, CloudAssemblySchema (product-branding PascalCase, per ServiceCatalog/AppConfig precedent). Nested submodules derive from their parent."
    },
